-- title:
--   Reduced fibres of a two-chart integral model over ℤ₍ₚ₎
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and write $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of those rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$. Let $F$ be a field equipped with a $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-algebra structure and let $j \in F$ be nonzero. Put $\mathcal{O}_{\mathrm{fin}} =$ `chartAlgFin`, the subalgebra of elements of $F$ integral over the $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-subalgebra generated by $j$, and $\mathcal{O}_{\mathrm{inf}} =$ `chartAlgInf`, the subalgebra of elements integral over the $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-subalgebra generated by $j^{-1}$. Assume both quotients $\mathcal{O}_{\mathrm{fin}}/(p)$ and $\mathcal{O}_{\mathrm{inf}}/(p)$, by the ideal generated by the image of the natural number $p$, are reduced rings. Let $\mathfrak{X} =$ `TwoChartIntegralModel`, the pushout in schemes of the two morphisms `fFin` and `fInf` out of the overlap chart `XMid` induced by the ring inclusions `inclFin`, `inclInf` of the two chart algebras, and let `toBase` $: \mathfrak{X} \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ be the morphism obtained from the pushout by descending the two structure morphisms. Then for every field $L$ and every ring homomorphism `toL` $: \mathbb{Z}_{(p)} \to L$, the fibre product of `toBase` with the induced map $\operatorname{Spec} L \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ is a reduced scheme.
--
--   This is a level-free form of the reducedness of the fibres of Igusa/Deligne–Rapoport style integral models of modular curves: chartwise reducedness modulo $p$ of the two integral closures forces reducedness of the base change to an arbitrary field over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$, in both the characteristic $p$ and the characteristic $0$ cases. It is used in the construction of generic charts for Atkin–Lehner twisted Deligne–Rapoport models, via [`ModularCurve.exists_xHDRModelAtP_atkinLehner_generic_chart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_xHDRModelAtP_atkinLehner_generic_chart).
